    "ls|LS16_S9_U_418": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n   MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE \n             DEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING & FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 418 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 19TH JULY, 2016 \nAGRICULTURAL/ANIMAL HUSBANDRY INSTITUTIONS \n \n418. SHRI SUKHBIR SINGH JAUNAPURIA \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE कृ षि एबं कृ िक कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has proposal to open Agricultural/Animal Husbandry  \ninstitutions in rural areas of the country including Rajasthan to enable the rural youth \nto get employment; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and  \n \n(c) the number of such colleges/ institutions opened by the Government during the last \nfive years and the details thereof, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n(SHRI SUDARSHAN BHAGAT) \n \n(a) to (c): Agriculture including Agriculture Education being a State subject, setting up of such \ninstitutions comes under the purview of the respective State Governm ent. However, to \nimprove the quality of research and for attaining excellence in specific strategic areas in \neducation and research and capacity building the State Agriculture Universities are being \nsupported in specific niche areas under the XII Plan Sche me “Strengthening and \nDevelopment of Higher Agricultural Education in India”.  \n           \n \n \n \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_419": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 419 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 19TH JULY, 2016/ ASHADHA 28, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nPROBE INTO PATHANKOT ATTACK CASE BY JIT \n \n†419.  SHRI KIRTI AZAD: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Joint Investigation Team (JIT) of Pakistan along with the \nemployees of Pakistani Intelligence agency, ISI visited  Pathankot and \nother places in the country  to probe the incident of terrorist attack on  \nPathankot Airbase; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof including  the details of the composition of \nthe Joint Investigation Team; \n \n(c) the justification for giving  permission to JIT along with ISI to probe  \nthe terrorist attack on Pathankot Airbase; and \n \n(d) the findings of the Joint Investigation Team? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) & (b):  A Five Member Joint Investigation Team (JIT) from Pakistan \nhad visited India between 27 th March, 2016 and 31 st March, 2016 to \ncollect, review and document physical evidences and to interview key \nwitnesses and victims , through the National Investigation Agency, with \nregard to the Pathankot Airbase terror attack .  The Five -Member JIT \ncomprised o f an Additional IGP, a DIG, two Lt. Colonels and one \nInspector.   \n...2/- \n\n-2- \nLS.US.Q.No. 419 FOR 19.07.2016 \n(c) &(d):  The Government of Pakistan constituted a Joint Investigation \nTeam (JIT) on 25 th February, 2016 under Section 19(I) of its Anti -\nTerrorism Act, 1997, to conduct investigation into an attack on \nPathankot Air Force base , in furtherance to an FIR registered at Police \nStation Counter -Terrorism Department (CTD), Gujranwala in Pakistan.  \nThe JIT informed that they were collecting admissible evidence outside \nPakistan under the provisions of the CrPC of Pakistan, that will legally \nenable them to use the evidence in prosecution. The interaction of JIT \nwith NIA was permitted in accordance with th e Terms of Reference \nmutually agreed on the basis of reciprocity. The exercise was aimed at \nproviding evidence to the JIT so that all those guilty of Pathankot attack \ncould be prosecuted effectively in Pakistan The NIA briefed the JIT on \ninvestigations car ried out in the Pathankot Airbase  terror attack.  The \nPakistan JIT, in turn, shared with NIA the results of investigations \ncarried out by them in Pakistan.  The Pakistan JIT assured of their full \ncooperation and promised to execute the LR, which had been r eceived \nby them.   \nThe findings of the JIT, if any, have not been shared with the \nGovernment of India, so far. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_420": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 420 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH JULY, 2016 \n \nFISH    PRODUCTION \n \n420.  SHRI SIRAJUDDIN AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE  कृषि और कृिक कल्याण मंत्री \n be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of quantum of fish production in the country at present State/UT wise; \n \n(b) the details including quantum of fish exported / imported by the country during the last three \nyears and the current year; \n \n(c) the details of per capita production of fish in the country at present State/UT-wise; and \n \n(d) the details of schemes / projects implemented by the Government for fish production in the \ncountry along with the details of amount spent / being spent on these schemes during  the last \nthree years and the current year, State/UT-wise? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n(SHRI SUDARSHAN BHAGAT) \n \n(a) The details of quantum of fish production in the country during 2015 -16, State/UT wise , is \nenclosed at Annexure – I. \n \n(b) The details of fish and fish products exported and imported by the country during the last three \nyears and the current year is enclosed at Annexure – II. \n \n(c) As per Census 2011 population, the per capita production of fish of the country as a whole during \n2015-16 works out to 8.87 Kg. The State/UT-wise estimations are enclosed at Annexure – III. \n \n(d) The Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Department of Animal Husbandry, Dairying \nand Fisheries was implementing the following schemes up  to 2015 -16 for development of \nfisheries and for production of fish in the country: \n \n(i) Development of Inland Fisheries and Aquaculture, \n(ii) Development of Marine Fisheries, Infrastructure and Post Harvest Operations, \n(iii) National Scheme of Welfare of Fishermen, \n(iv) Strengthening of Database and Geographical Information System of the Fisheries Sector, \n(v) National Fisheries Development Board (NFDB).  \n \nThe Department of Animal Husbandry, Dairying and Fisheries  has now restructured the \nfisheries schemes by merging all the fisheries schemes under an umbrella of a new Scheme \nnamely “Blue Revolution: Integrated Development and Management of Fisheries” . The newly \nrestructured scheme is being implemented from 2016 -17 with an outlay of Rs. 450 Crore for \n2016-17. \n \nThe details of funds released under the fisheries schemes during last 3 years and current year, \nState / UT wise are enclosed at Annexure – IV-A to IV-F.  \n \n**** \n\nAnnexure – I \n \nThe details of fish production in the country during 2015-16 (Provisional) \n \nS.No. States/UTs Fish Production in Tonnes \n1 Andhra Pradesh 2333427 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 4410 \n3 Assam 291692 \n4 Bihar 494579 \n5 Chhattisgarh 317334 \n6 Goa 115095 \n7 Gujarat 826295 \n8 Haryana 111200 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 10894 \n10 J & K 20294 \n11 Jharkhand 117987 \n12 Karnataka 695647 \n13 Kerala 680615 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 115387 \n15 Maharashtra 620955 \n16 Manipur 31266 \n17 Meghalaya 6140 \n18 Mizoram 6536 \n19 Nagaland 7835 \n20 Odisha 469709 \n21 Punjab 125340 \n22 Rajasthan 44353 \n23 Sikkim 443 \n24 Tamil Nadu 697612 \n25 Telangana 264234 \n26 Tripura 63560 \n27 Uttarakhand 3581 \n28 Uttar Pradesh 537936 \n29 West Bengal 1632178 \n30 A&N Islands 38292 \n31 Chandigarh 132 \n32 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 50 \n33 Daman & Diu 27751 \n34 Delhi 780 \n35 Lakshadweep 11949 \n36 Puducherry 70047 \n  Total 10795535 \n \n\nAnnexure – II \n \n \nThe details of fish and fish products exported and imported by the country \nduring the last three years and the current year \n \n \n \nYear \nImport Export \nQuantity \n(Kg) \nValue  \n(Rs.) \nQuantity  \n(Kg) \nValue  \n(Rs.) \n2013-14 1,77,32,951 270,57,29,019 111,10,49,935 29451,17,09,207 \n2014-15 2,35,96,586 379,29,12,908 112,50,22,763 32084,37,7